    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1070">

                <pb facs="1161" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1065"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-03-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 301.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 289, of 2d
                    instant, and to those preceding it on the same subject, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith a letter, which I received in the absence of the ambassador,
                    from Commander William Dawson, R. N., secretary to the Missions to Seamen,
                    transmitting a resolution of sympathy on the destruction of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine.</hi></p>
                <p>I immediately wrote him a letter of thanks in reply.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1070-a1.xml" xpointer="d1070-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
